38 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535001 true] [17592186325838 1111 #uuid "8520b09f-4c02-5433-84c4-2067d3793c08" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325839 1034 "-2" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535001 true] [17592186325839 1111 #uuid "df58f5f2-0605-56c6-a541-4df174d012cf" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325841 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1089 "q-275226" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1100 "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=8$, $|\\,d\\,|=5$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d$" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1113 #uuid "daea58c3-d874-52b1-9fd3-270fce74234d" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325840 1145 "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}d \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,d\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325842 13194139535001 true] [17592186325841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535001 true] [17592186325841 1041 "field-1" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325842 13194139535001 true] [17592186325841 1110 #uuid "13e10029-59bf-5a97-b9e9-494663c4d23e" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325842 1034 "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}" 13194139535001 true] [17592186325842 